# Code owners: who must approve a pull request before it can merge into main.
#
# GitHub only enforces this once main's protection rule has "Require review
# from Code Owners" turned on. Without it, owners are only auto-requested.
#
# Rules:
#   - The LAST matching line wins. Broad patterns first, specific ones below.
#   - Several owners on one line = any ONE of them can approve.
#   - A PR author cannot approve their own PR, so each department keeps the
#     founder as a second owner.
#   - Every owner needs write access to this repo.
#
# Keep in sync with _company/org-chart.md. scripts/validate.sh fails if a
# department folder has no line here. See setup/employee-onboarding.md.

# Fallback: everything not matched below is founder-only. That covers
# _company/, scripts/, skills/, integrations/, setup/, root files,
# departments/_template/, and .github/ (including this file).
*                          @naem2470

# Departments: one line per folder. When someone fills the role, put their
# GitHub username before the founder, e.g.
#   /departments/finance/  @finance-seat-username @naem2470
/departments/finance/      @naem2470
